{"availability":"available","full":"ine-labs/AzureGoat","name":"AzureGoat","description":"AzureGoat : A Damn Vulnerable Azure Infrastructure","category":"Other","language":"Python","stars":966,"forks":258,"created":"2022-08-09T17:54:54Z","updated":"2024-10-30T06:37:46Z","license":"MIT","branch":"master","homepage":null,"topics":[],"demo":"https://forum.defcon.org/node/242061","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T21:26:41.369Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T21:26:41.369Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T21:26:41.369Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-03T14:33:06.813Z","stars":967,"forks":257},{"at":"2026-10-04T16:12:05.883Z","stars":967,"forks":257},{"at":"2026-10-06T17:11:52.743Z","stars":966,"forks":257},{"at":"2026-10-08T21:26:41.369Z","stars":966,"forks":258}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Compromising an organization's cloud infrastructure is like sitting on a gold mine for attackers. And sometimes, a simple misconfiguration or a vulnerability in web applications, is all an attacker needs to compromise the entire infrastructure. Since the cloud is relatively new, many developers are not fully aware of the threatscape and they end up deploying a vulnerable cloud infrastructure. Microsoft Azure cloud has become the second-largest vendor by market share in the cloud infrastructure providers (as per multiple reports), just behind AWS. There are numerous tools and vulnerable…","AzureGoat is a vulnerable by design infrastructure on Azure featuring the latest released OWASP Top 10 web application security risks (2021) and other misconfiguration based on services such as App Functions, CosmosDB, Storage Accounts, Automation and Identities. AzureGoat mimics real-world infrastructure but with added vulnerabilities. It features multiple escalation paths and is focused on a black-box approach.","AzureGoat uses IaC (Terraform) to deploy the vulnerable cloud infrastructure on the user's Azure account. This gives the user complete control over code, infrastructure, and environment. Using AzureGoat, the user can learn/practice:"],"features":["Cloud Pentesting/Red-teaming","Detection and mitigation"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/ine-labs/AzureGoat/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"9a1e6c9896471e0f35f6ccee8c74336c50166bc96b00ddf8d81cf7917fecbbad","extractedAt":"2026-10-03T06:26:33.926Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T23:21:10.393Z","overviewRepoUpdated":"2024-10-30T06:37:46Z","lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T10:48:01.190Z","enrichmentAttemptAt":"2026-10-03T08:38:46.479Z","latestRelease":null,"releaseCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T08:38:46.479Z","screenshots":[{"src":"previews/b49e3f31914355068ec354c5.jpg","kind":"demo","capturedAt":"2026-10-04T18:18:24.092Z","url":"https://forum.defcon.org/node/242061"}],"projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Compromising an organization's cloud infrastructure is like sitting on a gold mine for attackers. And sometimes, a simple misconfiguration or a vulnerability in web applications, is all an attacker needs to compromise the entire infrastructure. Since the cloud is relatively new, many developers are not fully aware of the threatscape and they end up deploying a vulnerable cloud infrastructure. Microsoft Azure cloud has become the second-largest vendor by market share in the cloud infrastructure providers (as per multiple reports), just behind AWS. There are numerous tools and vulnerable…","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/ine-labs/AzureGoat/blob/master/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"To ease the deployment process the user just needs to clone this repo, login to azure cli then initialize and apply the Terraform file.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/ine-labs/AzureGoat/blob/master/README.md"},{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"And follow the steps to sign in.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/ine-labs/AzureGoat/blob/master/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"9a1e6c9896471